{"name":"Parasailing","hex":"#007d7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parasailing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A recreational activity where a person is towed behind a vehicle (usually a boat) while attached to a specially designed parachute, known as a parasail."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of parasail"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parasailing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parasailing","blocks":[{"text":"Parasailing, also known as parascending, is a water sport that involves a parafoil or modified parachute being towed behind a moving vehicle, so that the angle of attack at which the apparent wind flowing against the canopy will generate lift and carry passengers into the air. Commercial parasailing enterprises operate worldwide, and include customized powerboats that can seat numerous observers and up to three airborne parasailors at a time, wearing body harnasses and/or seated in a Customized Gondola."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Parasailing_from_a_yacht.jpg/330px-Parasailing_from_a_yacht.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parasailing","wikidata":"Q1194872"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/ParasailClose.jpg/500px-ParasailClose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/ParasailClose.jpg/500px-ParasailClose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chouteau's Old Mill Airlines, Westport, CT, 1981","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParasailClose.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/ParasailLong.jpg/500px-ParasailLong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki